# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: ryde-mat-fq-word-size
why: rbc_*_mat_fq_init allocates the matrix words, which are uint64_t, with sizeof(uint64_t *): the same
why: 8 bytes on 64-bit targets, but 4 bytes on 32-bit wasm32, so the matrix gets half the memory it uses
why: and the heap is overwritten (wasm32 abort in free from rbc_*_mat_fq_clear, CI run 45416349331).
why: The patch allocates sizeof(uint64_t) per word. 64-bit targets compile identical code.
file: upstream/ryde3s/src/rbc-61/rbc_61_mat_fq.c
count: 1
find: (*m)[0] = calloc(rows * words, sizeof(uint64_t *));
replace: (*m)[0] = calloc(rows * words, sizeof(uint64_t));
